From 4d857e958061809e2d28ccfce9db4ffc03433fcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:06:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] test(phone-pass): follow the home probe's new arguments
 and the phone context name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red at 917c70e:
  the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone › ⛔ POSITIVE — there is a pass at 390px, after the desktop walk (culprit 76f66a5d)
  the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone › ⛔ POSITIVE — every writer sets `bare`, and there are two of them (culprit 7b3111ab)

Root causes and decisions (both P):
- 76f66a5d gave the home probe a form scope and context:
  `probeControls(page, probeOpts('desktop:/', '/'))`; the anchor
  `probeOpts());` became -1. The 390px pass still follows the desktop walk
  (app-audit.ts 1125 -> 1347). The anchor is now the call's prefix.
- 7b3111ab renamed the phone writer's context 'phone:/' -> 'جوّال:/', the
  responsive sweep's own `${size.name}:${r}` key, so a completed phone pass
  owns that evidence and the duplicate sweep of '/' is skipped (P19).
  ProjectEditTool's FAQ check accepts both spellings. All three writers still
  set `bare: c.label`.

NOT changed: «⛔ POSITIVE — only controls the desktop walk never saw» stays
red. 7b3111ab deliberately records every ANCHOR in the phone pass even when
the desktop walk saw its label (live P19: the FAQ link was lost from phone
evidence). That contradicts the case's «only»; reported as a conflict.

Mutations (app-audit.ts, restored, sha256 identical each time):
  menu1 390px viewport set before the desktop walk -> ✕ Expected: > 62923  Received: 62870
  menu2 phone writer without `bare`                -> ✕ Expected substring "allControls.push({ ...c, bare: c.label, context: 'جوّال:/', …"

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 .../the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone.test.ts         | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/api/src/__tests__/the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone.test.ts b/api/src/__tests__/the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone.test.ts
index 708e7faf..ec3e5f3c 100644
--- a/api/src/__tests__/the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone.test.ts
+++ b/api/src/__tests__/the-menu-that-only-exists-on-a-phone.test.ts
@@ -46,7 +46,9 @@ describe('a control that only exists on a phone is pressed too', () => {
         //  After, not instead: the desktop walk is the main measurement and
         //  this pass exists for what desktop CANNOT show.
         expect(APP).toContain('await applyViewportSize(page, 390, 844);');
-        const walkAt = APP.indexOf('const homeProbe = await probeControls(page, probeOpts());');
+        //  The desktop walk is the home probe, whatever form scope it is
+        //  handed — `probeOpts()` grew a scope and a context for its forms.
+        const walkAt = APP.indexOf('const homeProbe = await probeControls(page, probeOpts(');
         const phoneAt = APP.indexOf('await applyViewportSize(page, 390, 844);');
         expect(walkAt).toBeGreaterThan(0);
         expect(phoneAt).toBeGreaterThan(walkAt);
@@ -93,7 +95,10 @@ describe('the decorated name and the real name are both kept', () => {
         //  same thing, one taught the rule and the other not. Both are asserted
         //  here because fixing either alone looks exactly like fixing both.
         expect(APP).toContain('allControls.push({ ...c, bare: c.label, context: `desktop:${route}`, label: route === \'/\' ? c.label : `${route} ${c.label}` })');
-        expect(APP).toContain("allControls.push({ ...c, bare: c.label, context: 'phone:/', label: `الجوّال ${c.label}` })");
+        //  The phone writer's context is named like the responsive sweep's
+        //  own (`${size.name}:${r}`, «جوّال:/»), so the two share one evidence
+        //  key; ProjectEditTool still accepts the older «phone:» spelling.
+        expect(APP).toContain("allControls.push({ ...c, bare: c.label, context: 'جوّال:/', label: `الجوّال ${c.label}` })");
         expect(APP).toContain('allControls.push({ ...c, bare: c.label, context: `${size.name}:${r}`, label, responsive: size.name })');
         //  …and nothing pushes a control without it.
         const pushes = APP.match(/allControls\.push\(\{[^}]*\}/g) || [];
